Author:&nbsp;<a href="mailto:&#107;&#114;&#121;&#120;&#64;&#98;&#114;&#105;&#115;&#116;&#108;&#101;&#98;&#97;&#110;&#101;&#46;&#99;&#111;&#109;?subject=Linkdeath">Kryx A'Tsunamu</a>&nbsp;(63.228.92.---)<br>
Date:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;02-09-01 12:51<br>
<br><HTML>Per the guide that refused my poor warrior's rez after ~another~ in a obscene string of LDs..<br>
<br>
"Linkdeath is part of the risk and realism of EQ".<br>
<br>
I take this to mean that all EQ characters must be afflicted with an epilepsy of some sort. Well.. im trying to rationalize.. how else could LD be a realistic feature.. maybe we all go catatonic from time to time.. were just fighting along and then all the sudden... glazed eyes and drool. It could happen. <br>
<br>
Right now the intrepid (if not very quiet) staff of Verant is claiming this to be a router problem.. but only if you sit in a chat room for long enough bearing through all the tantrums and idiots who want to educate you on the ins and outs of the unstable internet. I dont know what to believe only know that EQ is unplayable right now if your concerned about LD and the ramifications. <br>
<br>
My biggest beef with Verant concerning this is the lack of communication. Even with 500 angry customers in chat rooms freaking out Verant still has yet to put out a MOTD or any banner telling us what is going on. Poor communications cause problems to be worse then perhaps they are. The way they have handled this is reminicent of the poor service I endured in UO.. and we arent there anymore. We are paying customers and deserve to be treated as such in an open and honest manner by Verant.</HTML></font></tt><p>
